For any $y \in \mathbb{R}$, let $\cot^{-1}(y) \in (0, \pi)$ and $\tan^{-1}(y) \in \left(-\frac{\pi}{2}, \frac{\pi}{2}\right)$. Then the sum of all the solutions of the equation
$$\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{6y}{9-y^2}\right) + \cot^{-1}\left(\frac{9-y^2}{6y}\right) = \frac{2\pi}{3}$$
for $0 < |y| < 3$ is equal to:

50 mL of 0.2 molal urea solution (density = 1.012 g mL$^{-1}$ at 300 K) is mixed with 250 mL of a solution containing 0.06 g of urea. Both the solutions were prepared in the same solvent. The osmotic pressure (in Torr) of the resulting solution at 300 K is ___.

[Use: Molar mass of urea = 60 g mol$^{-1}$; gas constant, $R = 62$ L Torr K$^{-1}$ mol$^{-1}$;
Assume, $\Delta_{\text{mix}}H = 0, \Delta_{\text{mix}}V = 0$]
